  "instructions": [
    "Preheat oven to 375°F (190°C).",
    "Cut off the tops of the bell peppers and remove seeds and membranes.",
    "In a large skillet, heat oil over medium-high heat. Add onion and cook until softened.",
    "Add garlic, cumin, coriander, and cayenne pepper (if using) and cook for 1 minute.",
    "Stir in chili powder and cook for an additional minute.",
    "Stuff each bell pepper with the mixture and top with shredded cheese.",
    "Place peppers in a baking dish and cover with foil.",
    "Bake for 25 minutes, then remove foil and bake for an additional 10-15 minutes.",
    "Serve hot."
